import Mathlib
import Salt.Chen.SuperProfileDef

/-!
# SS3b — the `hSO` domination panels (odd-side numeric transcription)

Design: `docs/blueprints/flags.md`, `2026-07-13 SS2`/`SS3`.  Part 2 of the 3-way SS3
transcription split (SS3a = `SuperProfileDef.lean`, SS3c = the `hSE` side).  This file
discharges the odd-side super-solution inequality `hSO` that
`SuperSolution.massOSum_le_A1_of_superSolution` consumes, via `SuperProfile.hSO_reduce`.

## The obligation

`hSO`: for `w ≥ 1` and every top `b ≥ max w 3`,
`(1/w)·∫_{max w 3}^b Ebar(t-1) dt ≤ Obar w`.  Substituting `u = t-1` the integral is a tail
integral of the piecewise-linear `Ebar` profile plus the exact `K/v³` power tail.  `hSO_reduce`
removes the `∀ b` quantifier: it suffices to give a fixed rational bound `TE w` on the improper
tail (`hTE`) and check the panel-local inequality `(1/w)·TE w ≤ Obar w` (`hpt`).

## The structure

* `Ebar_int_L_a` — the exact partial-panel (trapezoid) forward integral of `Ebar`.
* `EbarCum`/`Ebar_cum_val` — the cumulative trapezoid head `∫_2^{2+m/20} Ebar` as an exact
  rational (one `by decide` recurrence over the 201-entry cumulative numerator list).
* `hSO_int_reduce` — `∫_{w-1}^{12} Ebar` as an explicit rational quadratic in `w` on each panel.
* `hSO_ppanel_0 … hSO_ppanel_179` — the 180 exact panels `w ∈ [3,12)` (each a rational quadratic
  `≥ 0`, `nlinarith`; all certified in `scripts/ss2_profile.py`, worst margin `2.8·10⁻¹⁰`).
* `hSO_flat_0 … hSO_flat_39` — the 40 flat panels `w ∈ [1,3)` (`max w 3 = 3`, constant tail `C`).
* `hpt_seam` (`w ∈ [12,13]`, `K ≥ 169·∫_{11}^∞ Ebar`), `hpt_tail` (`w > 13`, `(w-2)² ≥ 2`).
* `TEfun`/`hTE`/`hpt`/`hSO_holds` — the composition through `hSO_reduce`.

All values regenerated by `scripts/ss2_profile.py` (exact rationals, no floats in the certificate).
-/

